{
  "name": "pixel-pet",
  "vibe": "A handheld screen you can read across the room: #cfe8b8 mint LCD, #274029 pixels, one orange #e07a3f for alarm. Silkscreen bitmap caps over IBM Plex Mono, every beat uppercased, leading opened to 1.3 so lines read like status rows. The world is a 10-column dot grid at 12% opacity, a six-times-scaled sprite hopping on |sin(3t)| while gliding 220px each way, a pixel heart rising and fading above it, three ground blocks that jitter on a hard 2Hz step with no easing, and a white 6% scanline band sweeping down the frame. The camera translates only — zero rotation, zero skew — so pixels never smear. Mechanics: D-pad key presses, a segmented bar meter, side notifications, drag-to-feed. Best for games, toys, kids' apps and mascot-led products.",
